Hi Karim, how are you ?
The layer of tin formed by this chemical is not capable of protect the copper against corrosion in etching process, it only protect against oxidation from contact to the air. To create a etching protective layer you must use tin electoplating and an amonical etchant like ammonium hidroxide.]]></description>
			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Em resposta a <a href="https://www.engenhariacaseira.com.br/blog/?p=34#comment-412">karim saad</a>.</p>
<p>Hi Karim, how are you ?<br />
The layer of tin formed by this chemical is not capable of protect the copper against corrosion in etching process, it only protect against oxidation from contact to the air. To create a etching protective layer you must use tin electoplating and an amonical etchant like ammonium hidroxide.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
		
